From: =?UTF-8?q?Boris=20Sta=CC=88heli?= <ich@bstaehe.li>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:02:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] User button actions: act on hold start, lead-up melody
 ends at shutdown

- A hold of the user button runs the single press action as soon as it
  is recognized as a long press (~500 ms) instead of on release, so a
  hold until shutdown still sends the alert first. OneButton reports no
  click after a long press, so there is no double action.
- With long_press_shutdown_ms set, the stock lead-up melody is shifted so
  that it ends at the shutdown time and again means "release now to
  turn off".
- Drop the TX queue pre-check before sending the alert and ack texts:
  MeshPacketQueue::enqueue evicts lower-priority packets for these HIGH
  priority packets. The rate-limit window starts after sending.
---
 src/input/ButtonThread.cpp                  | 23 ++++++++++++++-------
 src/input/ButtonThread.h                    |  3 +++
 src/input/UserButtonActions.cpp             | 10 ++-------
 src/input/UserButtonActions.h               |  8 +++++++
 test/test_user_button_actions/test_main.cpp | 14 ++++++++++---
 5 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

